Karkov, whom the Weft call Kharkov and whose full name is Yuri Karkov, is a human [[Bestiary/Realmtouched#Duskwalker|Duskwalker]] of [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oresk]] and a general of the [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]]. He is an older man with blue skin, and he wears the deep blue uniform of the First House. Many people who agree with him follow him, and he has taken all three of the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]] bloods at once.

He raised two children as his wards, the elven woman called [[People/Althane/The Slipseer|the Slipseer]] and the orc [[People/Althane/Rampart|Rampart]] her brother, and kept them as his lieutenants. A locket in his desk holds their portraits as children. Both are now dead. He holds one of the few ultraviolet keycards to [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/RC3|RC3]], the installation he ran with [[People/Althane/Natalia|Natalia]], and during the crisis there the [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|Deep]] pressed on his mind, trying to drag him down into slumber. He meant to fight it, and his wounds close under a black silk like the one [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Nox|Nox]] binds with.

He has named [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]] the mongrels who killed his people, broke the beacon and stole the [[Phenomena/Althane/The Gun|gun]] the House kept, and their faces are going out in flyers across Oresk to be hunted down and hanged in the streets.

The Weft knew Karkov as a coworker, and hold that he does what he believes is best for everyone. They hold also that he is the champion of the Deep, whether he knows it or not. [[People/Althane/Masha|Masha]] says that if he is ever made to run, it will be to the bottom floor of the House's complex, where a passage leads off; she knows the passage only from its far end.
